# koku-family: 2 repos (project-koku/koku, Python; project-koku/koku-service-operator,
# Go) sharing one serena MCP daemon -- see
# launchd/io.vectorize.serena.koku-family.plist and
# launchd/io.vectorize.serena-multiplex.koku-family.plist for the daemon
# setup, and docs/findings/2026-08.md, 2026-08-17 entry, for the incident
# that prompted this (koku-service-operator's per-window stdio serena was
# apparently served by the sibling koku repo's already-running process
# instead of spawning its own -- most likely a Cursor stdio-MCP-client
# process-pooling quirk keyed on the unsubstituted server config).
#
# DAEMON_LABELS mirrors kubernaut-family.vars's reasoning exactly: only the
# daemon with real per-checkout file-state staleness risk goes here.
# io.vectorize.serena-multiplex.koku-family is a stateless relay (no cache
# of its own) and is deliberately excluded, same as kubernaut-family's
# multiplex.
FAMILY_NAME="koku-family"
DAEMON_LABELS="io.vectorize.serena.koku-family io.vectorize.serena-project-server"
DEBOUNCE_SECONDS=30
